For a true rate $n$ and dead time $\tau$, the recorded rate $m$ is
\begin{equation}
  m = \frac{n}{1+n\tau}\quad\text{(non-paralyzable)},\qquad
  m = n\,e^{-n\tau}\quad\text{(paralyzable)}.
  \label{eq:dt}
\end{equation}
We also fit a hybrid model, $m = n e^{-n\tau_2}/(1+n\tau)$

